<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 04:52:16 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil Supreme Court chief suspends rival rulings amid election row</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-brazil-supreme-court-chief-suspends-rival-rulings-amid-election-row</link><description>
Brazil's Supreme Court chief justice stepped in Wednesday to halt conflicting rulings by two fellow judges as a dispute over alleged links between Justice Alexandre de Moraes and a fraud-accused banker deepened. The clash has spilled into the campaign for next month's presidential election, adding to tensions around the court.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78dd3878-aca4-11f1-aedf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247600235559.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78dd3878-aca4-11f1-aedf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247600235559.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">73f60c82-aca8-11f1-b0c4-016c531905e6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 23:44:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78dd3878-aca4-11f1-aedf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247600235559.jpg">© Eraldo Peres, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Rubio to seek $45 million in additional security funding for Ecuador</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-rubio-to-seek-45-million-in-additional-security-funding-for-ecuador</link><description>
US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Wednesday that Washington would seek $45 million in additional security funding for Ecuador and provide military equipment as the two countries deepen cooperation against drug trafficking. During a visit to Quito, Rubio also announced new sanctions and a terrorist designation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32fa7e82-ac7d-11f1-9a34-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/a5421e17ec119b14a3a7062ebc329cd991951715.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32fa7e82-ac7d-11f1-9a34-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/a5421e17ec119b14a3a7062ebc329cd991951715.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f7348bf2-aca1-11f1-8eca-ed93256507d2</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 22:58:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32fa7e82-ac7d-11f1-9a34-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/a5421e17ec119b14a3a7062ebc329cd991951715.jpg">© Dolores Ochoa, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Trump 'believes in the power of his own charisma', analyst says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260909-trump-believes-in-the-power-of-his-own-charisma-analyst-says</link><description>
Republicans opened their highly unusual midterm convention in Dallas on Wednesday afternoon, a “Trump-a-Palooza” that is putting the president at the center of this fall’s midterm elections — whether the candidates running like it or not. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Professor Todd Belt, Director of the Political Management Programme at George Washington University, says that Trump "believes in the power of his own charisma".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02553b96-ac91-11f1-a87b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-223120-224354-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02553b96-ac91-11f1-a87b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-223120-224354-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce5dcefa-ac92-11f1-926b-4f97f44a989b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 21:09:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Trump claims firefighters carried him to safety ‘right after’ 9/11, but his account is disputed</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-claims-firefighters-carried-him-to-safety-right-after-9-11-but-his-account-is-disputed-1</link><description>
As the 25th anniversary of 9/11 approaches, Donald Trump has lashed out at the press over coverage questioning where he was. This week, he said two firefighters carried him to safety near the US Steel Building right after the attacks, though he later said that he wasn’t at the World Trade Center on the day of the collapse. His version of events, and alleged role at Ground Zero have evolved many times over the years, as Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c458f60e-ac8e-11f1-a3bb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8387411906aa1c45bec0901-48181484.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c458f60e-ac8e-11f1-a3bb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8387411906aa1c45bec0901-48181484.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a0bba7f0-ac8e-11f1-8fe7-fb408532d069</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 20:52:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Republicans put Trump center stage in US midterms gamble</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/republicans-put-trump-center-stage-in-us-midterms-gamble</link><description>
US Republicans open an extraordinary midterm convention in Dallas on Wednesday betting that putting Donald Trump at the center of their campaign can rescue a party facing grim election forecasts -- despite the president's deeply negative approval ratings. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e568c03a-ac67-11f1-94b2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T030521Z-656306742-RC2OYK97ENYA-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-REPUBLICANS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e568c03a-ac67-11f1-94b2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T030521Z-656306742-RC2OYK97ENYA-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-REPUBLICANS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1c6b8226-ac80-11f1-b60f-f77bcad93d74</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 19:04:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>How a French Foreign Legion soldier dramatically escaped Colombian captors</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-how-a-french-foreign-legion-soldier-dramatically-escaped-colombian-captors</link><description>
A French Foreign Legion soldier kidnapped by Colombian guerrillas escaped after nearly a month in captivity by overpowering a guard, jumping into a river with his hands tied and trekking for four days through the Andes to reach safety, according to a Colombian military source.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cbe6028-ac66-11f1-94f1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7LM6NQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cbe6028-ac66-11f1-94f1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7LM6NQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">24c2d00e-ac68-11f1-86c7-8d898541b3b4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 16:17:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cbe6028-ac66-11f1-94f1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7LM6NQ.jpg">© Handout via Colombian Military Forces, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Rubio hails Colombia's new pro-Trump leader De la Espriella on first stop of Latin American tour</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-rubio-hails-colombia-new-pro-trump-leader-de-la-espriella-first-stop-of-latin-american-tour</link><description>
US Secretary of State Marco Rubio pledged closer security cooperation with Bogota on the first stop of his three-nation tour of pro-Washington Latin American nations. Rubio hailed the election of Colombian President Abelardo De La Espriella as part of a growing alignment with US interests across the Western Hemisphere.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e584ada-abcc-11f1-a27a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-08T212234Z-1495157115-RC28FNAWLXD4-RTRMADP-3-USA-COLOMBIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e584ada-abcc-11f1-a27a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-08T212234Z-1495157115-RC28FNAWLXD4-RTRMADP-3-USA-COLOMBIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8980e2f2-ac12-11f1-b389-b192a62acd88</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 06:27:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e584ada-abcc-11f1-a27a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-08T212234Z-1495157115-RC28FNAWLXD4-RTRMADP-3-USA-COLOMBIA.jpg">© Fernando Vergara, Pool via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US bans Canadian alcohol, motorcycles and dairy products as trade spat escalates</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-us-bans-canadian-alcohol-motorcycles-and-dairy-products-as-trade-spat-escalates</link><description>
The US and Canada escalated a bitter trade dispute on Tuesday, with Washington imposing new import bans on Canadian alcohol, motorcycles and dairy products as Ottawa's retaliatory tariffs on US goods took effect.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db134d28-abed-11f1-8986-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/0a11131be75eaa75c2e6b179bfeca995a738f844.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db134d28-abed-11f1-8986-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/0a11131be75eaa75c2e6b179bfeca995a738f844.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">395e8060-abf7-11f1-b670-ad598986f6fc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 02:36:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db134d28-abed-11f1-8986-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/0a11131be75eaa75c2e6b179bfeca995a738f844.jpg">© Alex Wroblewski, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>New York City releases post-9/11 air toxicity information kept secret for 25 years</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-key-post-9-11-air-toxicity-information-was-kept-secret-for-25-years</link><description>
New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani on Tuesday announced the release of tens of thousands of documents detailing what city officials knew about toxic air after the September 11 attacks as the 25th anniversary approaches and thousands still suffer from related illnesses. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85878ca4-abaa-11f1-ad9b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Part-GTY-2294151191-1-1-0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85878ca4-abaa-11f1-ad9b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Part-GTY-2294151191-1-1-0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fb64a25a-abef-11f1-baf0-ad598986f6fc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 01:44:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85878ca4-abaa-11f1-ad9b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Part-GTY-2294151191-1-1-0.jpg">© Michael M. Santiago, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Smithsonian chief steps down amid Trump pressure over how US history is presented</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-smithsonian-chief-lonnie-bunch-steps-down-amid-trump-administration-pressure</link><description>
The Smithsonian announced Tuesday that Secretary Lonnie Bunch will leave his post at the end of the year as the institution faces continued scrutiny from the Trump administration over how its museums present US history.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d5734f8c-abdc-11f1-b5e7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2262709064.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d5734f8c-abdc-11f1-b5e7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2262709064.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ee70c810-abe2-11f1-afcc-31f619116af0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 00:10:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d5734f8c-abdc-11f1-b5e7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2262709064.jpg">© Anna Moneymaker, Getty Images via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Accelerating diversification: Canada seeks economic sovereignty amid Trump's 'nonsensical' posturing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260908-accelerating-diversification-canada-seeks-economic-sovereignty-amid-trump-s-nonsensical-posturing</link><description>
FRANCE 24’s François Picard speaks with Jean Simard, President and CEO of the Aluminum Association of Canada. According to Simard, the US-Canada aluminum dispute is not a conventional disagreement over trade, but rather a 'Trump posture that makes no sense". As American industrial demand substantially exceeds domestic production capacity, tariffs will do nothing to reduce Canadian aluminum from the US market. Protectionism does not eliminate interdependence, explains Simard, it makes that interdependence considerably more expensive.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9eb3b5ec-abc6-11f1-9f50-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7478268466aa074913d3230-92407640.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9eb3b5ec-abc6-11f1-9f50-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7478268466aa074913d3230-92407640.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9328d552-abc8-11f1-be7f-43659e3dc167</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 21:02:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Trump posts AI map showing US 'takeover' of North America, Iceland and Caribbean</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-posts-ai-map-showing-us-takeover-of-north-america-iceland-and-caribbean-1</link><description>
US President Donald Trump shared an AI-generated map Monday appearing to show the US absorbing Canada, Mexico, Greenland, Iceland, Cuba and parts of the Caribbean into a giant “United States of America”. Shared without context, the post sparked diplomatic backlash. Iceland summoned its ambassador and Mexico defended its sovereignty. Denmark also pushed back over Greenland. Online, the map has triggered widespread ridicule and questions about Trump’s fitness for office.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c842adea-abb8-11f1-96f5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-19967755976aa05d5a31b434-89704745.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c842adea-abb8-11f1-96f5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-19967755976aa05d5a31b434-89704745.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">911855c2-abb8-11f1-ac89-31b675c94139</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 19:43:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Canada will move faster from US reliance as tariffs take effect and Trump response looms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/canada-will-move-faster-from-us-reliance-as-tariffs-take-effect-and-trump-response-looms</link><description>
Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said Tuesday that Canada would move faster to reduce its economic reliance on the United States as retaliatory tariffs took effect on about $20 billion worth of U.S. goods and the country braced for President Donald Trump’s response. FRANCE 24's Christopher Guly reports from Ottawa.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e49123dc-a087-11f1-8dc3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T163056Z-1186857443-RC2R3NAM318W-RTRMADP-3-CANADA-DEFENSE-ICEBREAKERS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e49123dc-a087-11f1-8dc3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T163056Z-1186857443-RC2R3NAM318W-RTRMADP-3-CANADA-DEFENSE-ICEBREAKERS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">128c31f8-abb6-11f1-9f4a-cb5378abc52f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 19:19:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'US Midterm elections tend to be referendums on the unpopularity of the president'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-tend-to-be-referendums-on-the-unpopularity-of-the-president</link><description>
Annette Young is pleased to welcome Michelle Swers, Professor of Government at Georgetown University. She frames the New Hampshire primary as both a major Senate contest and an unusually strong indication of the national political climate ahead of November. While Democrats face a difficult Senate map and cannot afford to surrender an open seat they already hold, the broader midterm political environment might become a referendum on President Donald Trump’s performance. New Hampshire is particularly instructive because its closely divided electorate makes national political currents more visible. Swers argues that Trump’s low approval and the local economic consequences of tariffs on Canada create significant headwinds for Republicans, especially in a state whose political identity is strongly associated with resistance to taxation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe2ff40-ab9e-11f1-a32a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-130757-131402-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe2ff40-ab9e-11f1-a32a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-130757-131402-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a565ad1e-ab9e-11f1-9fb0-51605c18cb6e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 16:25:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US war on Iran: 'Incompetent administration when it comes to negotiations and prosecuting war'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war</link><description>
Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Simpson Center. She frames the war in the Persian Gulf as a mutually damaging stalemate in which neither Washington nor Tehran has found a politically sustainable exit: "There are no winners in this war". Her central argument is that the conflict has created a problem of face-saving as much as military strategy. The US faces rising economic and electoral costs, while Iran confronts shortages, inflation, domestic dissent and intensified repression. Neither side, in her assessment, can plausibly claim success.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b728f026-ab9c-11f1-a25d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-211527-212306-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b728f026-ab9c-11f1-a25d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-211527-212306-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bd10da6c-ab9c-11f1-ae90-d5d37e7d97b0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 16:16:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Rubio kicks off tour in Latin America as US vies for regional influence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-rubio-begins-latin-america-tour-in-colombia-to-secure-us-influence</link><description>
United States Secretary of State Marco Rubio on Tuesday arrived in Colombia following the recent election of hard-right lawyer and US ally President Abelardo de la Espriella, and a string of right-wing electoral victories across Latin America. Colombia is the first stop on a tour designed to bolster pro-US leaders and cement influence over the continent.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6872607c-ab4a-11f1-8df8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/e0dd1f1f8a170e5c07e77666fa254fb6526d908a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6872607c-ab4a-11f1-8df8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/e0dd1f1f8a170e5c07e77666fa254fb6526d908a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">69d166f2-ab4a-11f1-871e-15a88be1190e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 05:59:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6872607c-ab4a-11f1-8df8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/e0dd1f1f8a170e5c07e77666fa254fb6526d908a.jpg">© Kent Nishimura, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Canada's counter-tariffs take effect on several US goods as trade war reignites</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-canada-s-counter-tariffs-take-effect-on-several-us-goods-as-trade-war-reignites</link><description>
Canada's counter-tariffs on billions of dollars in US products took effect Tuesday, as a trade war between the two countries heated up. Ottawa's pushback comes weeks after US President Donald Trump imposed 50-percent tariffs on a similar value of Canadian products, over what Washington deemed as "discriminatory treatment" against US alcohol, automobile and dairy industries.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/815aca80-ab3a-11f1-9564-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/6899456a8cc8b1fba9918fa141a4437630c8ce44.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/815aca80-ab3a-11f1-9564-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/6899456a8cc8b1fba9918fa141a4437630c8ce44.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3717d1d4-ab3a-11f1-be44-670dee264cb9</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 04:03:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/815aca80-ab3a-11f1-9564-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/6899456a8cc8b1fba9918fa141a4437630c8ce44.jpg">© Andrej Ivanov, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump threatens to ban Canadian Bombardier jets from US market</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-trump-ban-canadian-bombardier-jets-us-market</link><description>
US President Donald Trump threatened on Monday to block sales of Canadian planemaker Bombardier in the United States unless it builds aircraft in the country, escalating trade tensions on the eve of Canadian retaliatory tariffs. Trump accused Canada of “unjust and unfair” trade practices but did not explain how a ban would work.
